## K-r16.1-D1 — a degree-1 exact pin of `V_U(w*)` on the h=1024 rung (theorem + exhaustive real-prime sweep)

**Killed** r16.1, 2026-09-13. **Seat** soulbis (Opus) at probe 5 (and probe 9 on a proposer slip);
critic: structural.

**The claim.** A third root `w* ∈ K \ {0}` whose value `V_U(w*)` is confined jointly with the
product key `V_U(0) ∈ μ_256` to a subgroup of index ≥ 8 (`e = m·c`, `m = [K^* : Γ(w*)]`,
`c` = the Goursat common quotient), making the third root cost ≤ 531391578 instead of `p−1`.

**The kill.** The joint index is exactly 1 for every `w ∈ K \ {0}` at degree 1: the Goursat
reduction `e = m·c`, then an exhaustive sweep over all 2,130,706,433 points of `K` at
`H = 256` (also 512 and 1024) with survivors `U2 = {0}`, `T2 = none` — reproduced by the prover's
own QR-table sweep (27.7 s build + 76.9 s sweep) and by a brute-force arbiter over every
character pair of `μ_H × K^*` (0 counterexamples at `q = 113/193/769/12289`, controls to the
digit). Hence the third root costs `p−1` and the count is 68579341057697257 < `bar` by 2.003485
bits. Also on record: the proposal's Lean entry lemma `orbit_count` as written
(`(p^5·256·I)·2^59 < choose 255 136`) is FALSE for `I = 266338304` (largest admissible `I` under
`2^59` is 253482032); the correct constant is `2^58` (largest `I` 506964064, and `2^58 > bar`).

**Re-open condition.** (i) a multi-point additive functional `Σ c_i V_U(w_i)` with a proven image
≤ 531391578 at the real `p` (currently only birthday-sampled on 10^6 subsets, consistent with
image `p`); or (ii) a `w*` in `F = K^6 \ K` with a proven small image whose prescription costs
fewer than 29 bits of keyspace (`push_r4.residual_open`: closed by 16 analogues, not exhaustion);
or (iii) a key ledger for the rung that does not charge the third root as a generic `K`-root at
all — none priced by any r15/r16 lens. Evidence: `runs/r16.1/r16.1.1/propose-index8-exact-pin-theory/`
(`twist_d1.c`, `ledger.mjs`), `runs/r16.1/r16.1.1/p2-index8-exact-pin-closure-d1/`.

