## K-r15.1-SA — seven agreements on the h=512 OrbitPencil shape (off-lattice agreement gain)

**Killed** r15.1, 2026-09-13. **Seat** soulbis (Opus) at probe 5; critic: structural.

**The claim.** Cut a sub-family of the live max-key fibre (`G = ceil(C(511,272)/(512·p^14)) =
4009245024241067461`) sharing seven further agreement points, retaining `>= 6.8586661 %`,
to reach index 122362 / 11612.

**The kill.** On the 512-fibred shape agreement moves in whole fibres: `f1 + γ_U·f2 − c_U =
RF(x)·V_U(x^512)/(z(z−α))` on the whole domain, so a point agrees iff `RF(x) = 0` or
`V_U(x^512) = 0`, and `m ≡ 131071 (mod 512)` is forced. 139782 ≡ 131071 + 7 is off-lattice by
construction; the +7 and the +512 are the same event (core `>= 518 > 511`). Any cutting
invariant must have `<= 14` values (`ceil(G/14) > bar`, `ceil(G/15) < bar`); every named
mechanism is 27.12–57.93 bits short (15th K-pin 1881650594; `β = α^p` cap 2130706433;
lattice a=273 J=15 1647305831; μ_2/4/8/16 32186199/7074371/5569676/8286954; shared off-domain
F-root 1). `f2_far` ledger: core 1023 with 14 pins = 132095 > 131583 breaks; the 15th pin is
mandatory; live rung 511 + 512·256 = 131583, zero slack.

**Re-open condition.** A functional of `U` on the h=512 shape whose image has `<= 14` values
(a coset of the order-2/4/8 subgroup of `K^*`, `p−1 = 2^24·127`) AND whose vanishing or
membership forces one agreement point off the 512-lattice, with an exact image-size proof in
characteristic `p`. Evidence: `runs/r15.1/r15.1.1/p1-seven-agreements-lattice-closure-h512/`.

