## K-r15.1-AA — an accounting wider than one instance (averaging, pairs)

**Killed** r15.1, 2026-09-13. **Seat** soulbis (Opus) at probe 5; critic: structural
(definition-shaped).

**The claim.** Recover the 2.0035 bits at 121857 by averaging over pencil sources, counting
colliding pairs, or any `winningSetDensity` entry point wider than one instance.

**The kill.** `winningSetDensity` is an `iSup` over single `ViolatingInstance`s
(`SoundnessBounds.lean:1146-1148` at clone 207eb22); every ArkLib lower bound (`:1193`, `:1224`,
`KnowledgeSoundness:396`) terminates in `winningSetRatio_le_winningSetDensity` on ONE
instance; `Λ`, `epsPg`, `epsCa` are likewise sups over one centre / one WordStack. For a
pencil-shaped source the winning set IS one key fibre, so the pigeonhole yields only
`max >= mean = ceil(C(255,136)/(256·p^6)) = 68579341025511059 = 2^55.928624`; `bar/mean =
4.009672` — **exactly the 2.0035 bits.** The second-moment escape needs `Var/mean^2 >=
3.009672`, and productKey uniformity is closed (Ramanujan, `2^-127.14`, push_r4).

**Re-open condition.** An upstream ArkLib change (new clone commit) that lower-bounds
`winningSetDensity` by an average or a pair count; or an explicit key fibre of the h=1024
J=6 a=136 joint key of size `>= 274980728111395088` exhibited directly (equivalently
`Var/mean^2 >= 3.009672` for that key map). Evidence:
`runs/r15.1/r15.1.1/p3-alt-accounting-closure-sup-over-single-instance/`.

