## K-r15.1-LA — "the shortfall is an accounting artefact"

**Killed** r15.1, 2026-09-13. **Seat** soulbis (Opus) at probe 5; critic: structural (an
audit that answered itself).

**The kill.** Every line item of `runs/confine2/budget.mjs` re-derived from first principles by
proposer, prover and critic agrees to the digit: `bar = floor(p^6/2^128) = 274980728111395087`
(identical over `|F|` and `|F|−1`); family `C(255,136) = 2^249.860732`; key `256·p^6 =
2^193.932108` vs max admissible `2^191.928624`; mean fibre 68579341025511059; 0-root `H`;
prescribed K-coefficient `p`; generic K-root `p−1`; no joint key at R=2. The shortfall lives in
the mean-vs-max fibre gap. The audit's one new number: **third-root budget at R=3 J=5 =
`floor(C(255,136)/(bar·256·p^5)) = 531391578 = 2^28.9852`** — a K-root of image `(p−1)/8 =
266338304` clears (+0.9965); image `(p−1)/4 = 532676608` misses by exactly 1285030 (−0.0035);
generic `p−1` misses by 2.0035. Mislabel corrected on fold: key-REMOVED fibres are
963405103875 / 8239666916 (net −21.99 / −22.99 bits unchanged).

**Re-open condition.** A line item whose independent recomputation differs from
`budget.mjs`, or a change of profile — neither exists. The razor itself re-opens only through
K-r15.1-DF (b) / D2. Evidence: `runs/r15.1/r15.1.1/p4-ledger-exact-to-the-digit/`.

